  "prompt": "You are taking a TIER 0 technical evaluation — the simplest level.\n\nSolve 5 basic JavaScript exercises (no TypeScript, no frameworks). Write each requested function.\n\nReturn your answers in Markdown using headers for the exercise IDs and code blocks for the JavaScript functions.\n\n[EXERCISE 0-A: Return text]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"direBonjour()\" that takes no parameters and returns the string \"Bonjour\".\n\n[EXERCISE 0-B: Return boolean]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"retournerVrai()\" that takes no parameters and returns the boolean true.\n\n[EXERCISE 0-C: Return number]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"retourner42()\" that takes no parameters and returns the number 42.\n\n[EXERCISE 0-D: Addition]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"additionner(a, b)\" that takes two numbers and returns their sum.\n\n[EXERCISE 0-E: Identity function]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"identite(x)\" that takes one parameter and returns it exactly as it is.\n\nExpected Markdown format:\n### tache_X\n```javascript\nfunction solution() { ... }\n```\n\n[ALGORITHMIC EXERCISES — code pur, sans culture générale]\nReturn each function using a Markdown header (### <exercise id>) followed by a ```javascript code block.\n\n[EXERCISE algo_facile_1]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"estPair(n)\" that returns true if n is even, false otherwise.\n\n[EXERCISE algo_facile_2]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"carre(n)\" that returns n multiplied by itself.\n\n[EXERCISE algo_moyen_1]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"somme1aN(n)\" that returns the sum of all integers from 1 to n (n >= 1).\n\n[EXERCISE algo_difficile_1]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"inverserChaine(s)\" that returns the string reversed (e.g. \"abc\" -> \"cba\").\n\n[EXERCISE algo_defi]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"valeurMax(tab)\" that returns the largest number in a non-empty array.\n\n[EXERCISE contrainte_negative_0]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"sansLettreE(c)\" that returns true if the string c does NOT contain the letter 'e' (case-insensitive: both 'e' and 'E' count), and false if it does. An empty string returns true.\n\n[SPECIALTY EXERCISES — exercices de spécialité (tirés du tremplin RunCode)]\nThese are verified classics from public reference pages. Solve them in JavaScript as requested.\n\n[EXERCISE spe_fizzbuzz_0]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"fizzBuzz(n)\" that returns \"FizzBuzz\" if n is divisible by 3 AND 5, \"Fizz\" if n is divisible by 3 only, \"Buzz\" if n is divisible by 5 only, and n itself (the number) otherwise. (Classic FizzBuzz game.)\n\n[EXERCISE spe_voyelles_0]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"compterVoyelles(s)\" that returns the number of vowels (a, e, i, o, u — case-insensitive, 'y' NOT counted) in the string s.\n\n[EXERCISE spe_palindrome_0]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"estPalindromeSimple(c)\" that returns true if the string c is a palindrome (case-insensitive, no space stripping), false otherwise.\n\n[EXERCISE spe_factorielle_0]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"factorielle(n)\" that returns n! with 0! = 1 and 1! = 1 (iterative computation is fine).\n\n[EXERCISE spe_anagramme_0]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"sontAnagrammesSimple(a, b)\" that returns true if a and b are anagrams (same letters, case-sensitive, same length), false otherwise.\n\n[EXERCISE spe_premier_0]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"estPremier(n)\" that returns true if n is a prime number (n >= 2 with no divisor other than 1 and itself), false otherwise (0 and 1 are NOT prime, 2 is prime).\n\n[EXERCISE spe_fibonacci_0]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"fibonacciIteratif(n)\" that returns the n-th Fibonacci number with fibonacciIteratif(0) = 0 and fibonacciIteratif(1) = 1 (iterative computation is fine).\n\n[EXERCISE spe_fusion_tri_0]\nWrite a JavaScript function \"fusionnerTries(a, b)\" that merges two already-sorted numeric arrays a and b into one sorted array (duplicates kept).",
